From: OpenWrt
Subject: [PATCH] allwinner: h616: restore PMIC I2C mode when probing fails

sunxi_pmic_setup() unconditionally switches the PMIC from I2C to RSB mode
before it reads the chip ID. When the ID does not match the AXP305 the
function bails out early, several lines before the "switch the PMIC back to
I2C mode" write, so the PMIC is left on RSB for the rest of the boot.

Boards with a different PMIC (e.g. the AXP15060 on the Teleofis RTU1068v5,
which reports ID 0x44) are then unreachable on R_I2C for both U-Boot proper
and Linux: the regulators never register, and every consumer of them -
pinctrl supplies, MMC, EMAC - stays in deferred probe forever.

Put the PMIC back into I2C mode on the error path as well. The RSB runtime
address has already been assigned at that point, so the write goes through;
if RSB failed earlier the write simply fails and the original error is
still returned.

--- a/plat/allwinner/sun50i_h616/sunxi_power.c
+++ b/plat/allwinner/sun50i_h616/sunxi_power.c
@@ -79,6 +79,13 @@ int sunxi_pmic_setup(uint16_t socid, cons
 	ret = rsb_init();
 	if (ret) {
 		INFO("Could not init RSB: %d\n", ret);
+		/*
+		 * The PMIC has already been switched to RSB mode above, so put
+		 * it back into I2C mode before bailing out, otherwise U-Boot
+		 * and the kernel can no longer reach it on the R_I2C bus.
+		 */
+		axp_write(AXP20X_MODE_REG, AXP20X_MODE_I2C);
+
 		return ret;
 	}

